        "original_id": "a145b1ac-7860-5d58-8e4d-f4dd9ca01b14",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: British Airways, BA CityFlyer, Sun Air, Comair, KLM, Kenya Airways\n- Places: OR Tambo International Airport, Johannesburg, Cape Town International Airport, King Shaka International Airport\n- Topics: British Airways franchise destinations, airline ownership stakes, airline bases and focus cities\n\nFacts:\n- British Airways franchise carriers Sun Air and Comair, together with wholly owned subsidiary BA CityFlyer, operate aircraft in full British Airways livery, offer full British Airways service, and have staff who wear British Airways uniforms.\n- Comair's main base is OR Tambo International Airport in Johannesburg.\n- Comair has focus cities at Cape Town International Airport and King Shaka International Airport.\n- British Airways has an 18% stake in Comair.\n- KLM has a 26% stake in Kenya Airways.",
